WEBVTT

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.870
I didn't get a chance to let Honoka know
that I would be late.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.290
I'm back...

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.910
It's not opening...?

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.750
Come on...!

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.000
Huh? What are you doing?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.160
Uh... I think it's called "punishment"?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.700
Ao, you traitor!

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.660
You said you'd help me keep Ikuto out!

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.750
Who's going to fix the doorknob when it breaks?

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.750
--Sorry, sorry, sorry.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.540
Hey, could you guys keep it down?

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:54.580
Hey. Dinner's almost ready,
so let's wash our hands.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.500
H-Honoka.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.330
Last night...

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.450
What were you doing last night?

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:05.700
Um... I was helping out at Mr. Yanagida's...

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.160
You got another part-time job
and spent the night without letting us know?

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.500
S-Sorry.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.250
For what?

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.330
She's livid.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.750
You could've called at least.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.750
It was too late when I thought to call,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:20.120
--and my battery died this morning.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.790
--Iku's full of excuses.
--and my battery died this morning.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.910
--Iku's full of excuses.
--Then more things happened...

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.000
--Sounds like it.
--Then more things happened...

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.120
Um... Let me help out with dinner!

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.410
You're a terrible cook. Just sit down.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.040
"Hayasaka General Hospital"

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:04.660
"Hayasaka General Hospital"
"Episode 4: Young Talents"

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.040
"Episode 4: Young Talents"

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.750
"Episode 4: Young Talents"
Are you working again, Ms. Tsumura?

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.830
But this isn't work!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.000
Please don't forget that you're here
because you overworked.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.910
You can't keep working like this!

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.200
But this isn't work-- Oh, he's back.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.000
Just please don't overdo it.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.250
Duly noted!

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.330
Let's listen to the nurse, okay?

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.790
Okay, okay.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.160
Anyway, Ikuto,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.450
have you noticed how Honoka's
on edge these days?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:39.660
Her grades fell so her professor advised
her to attend summer school.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.200
Oh. I see...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.830
I wonder if Mr. Yanagida's going to pay me...

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.200
Ikuto?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.620
Sorry, Mother. I have to go.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.450
Oh? But you just got here.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.620
I have to get to work. I'll see you tomorrow!

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.910
Mother.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.290
You don't have to tell Ikuto everything.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.080
I just hate seeing you guys fight.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.750
The moment you get angry you stop wearing
the clothes your brother made for you.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:17.950
He always uses a check pattern
in your clothes, so I could tell right away.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.000
Your mock exam scores weren't great, right?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000
It doesn't matter. I'm not going to college.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.790
Here, use this to pay for summer school.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.750
But...

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.790
Don't worry. Just take it.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.290
This is for you.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.660
Okay...

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.450
Ikuto's more sensitive than you are.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:41.540
He needs your support, too.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.450
How long has it been since we last heard him say

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.580
that he wants to become a designer?

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.040
Hey. Why do you want to be a designer?

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.450
Huh? Well, um...

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:59.160
"We'd like to invite you to an exhibit where our brand,
Hazime Yanagida, will be featured. The details are below..."
Because I like to make clothes...? I guess.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:04:59.580
Because I like to make clothes...? I guess.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.040
You didn't always want to be a designer.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.950
So what happened?

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.200
It's a long story...

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.870
You won't last in this industry
if you just "like" it.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.620
Designers handle all sorts of tasks
you're not aware of.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:19.870
You have to handle the demands of deadlines,
quality standards, and creativity.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.660
If you fail, you'll be treated harshly.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.290
The day will come when you'll hate it.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.790
You need to find a reason
beyond just "liking" it,

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.120
or else all you'll face is defeat.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.250
What do I truly want...?

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.830
Her professor advised her
to attend summer school.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.660
What are your aspirations, Mr. Yanagida?

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.580
What? Mine?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.540
Mine are...

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.870
...to be featured in Paris Fashion Week.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.620
And for "Hazime Yanagida"
to be recognized by the world.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.540
Bob. What are your aspirations?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.790
Um, Mr. Yanagida.

00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.660
What? You're begging for more scraps?

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.580
Y-Yes...

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.410
No.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:19.200
If you're going to beg for them...

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.750
Go buy them yourself.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:30.370
This is my favorite café.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.200
Yes, it's my treasure.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.660
This is so cute!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.040
That pattern's called check!

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.120
I'm back.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.660
Sorry, I know it's late.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.290
Where're Ichika and Aoi?

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.500
They're asleep.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.040
Did I disrupt your study session?

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.450
Want me to make you some coffee?

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.080
I don't want any.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.120
Honoka, could I talk to you for a second?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.580
Here.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.660
"Tsumura Paycheck"

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.950
"Tsumura Paycheck"
What's that?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.660
"Tsumura Paycheck"
It's from helping out at Mr. Yanagida's.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.040
"Tsumura Paycheck"
He just paid me.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.000
You need to stop doing this!

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.250
What?

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.580
I'm responsible for myself!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.660
You always put everyone else first, Ikuto!

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.290
You're the one sacrificing your dream
by choosing to work.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:27.250
There's no way I could go
to college with that money!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.700
If I'm going, I'll make it happen by myself.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.540
I don't need your help, Ikuto.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:39.620
Realizing my dream at the expense
of others won't make me happy.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.910
Iku, Noka, what's going on?

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:47.790
Noka, are you crying?

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.540
Ichika?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.000
There!

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.200
Change, Noka!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:03.700
Wearing Iku's clothes always makes Ichika smile!

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:08.080
When Mommy doesn't come home,
or Iku comes back late,

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.330
it makes me feel better and not sad.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.290
So let's change.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:16.620
When you change, you'll stop crying...

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:26.080
It's not like that, Honoka.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.540
Mr. Yanagida is a professional designer.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:32.330
And I'm learning a lot while working for him.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.830
What?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:37.290
And so I got my first paycheck today.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:41.000
He told me, "If you want to earn more,
then you need to improve more."

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.080
He's strict, but it's been really fulfilling.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:48.910
So I'm not forcing myself
to take up a part-time job.

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.830
Are you... serious...?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:54.870
So I was wrong this whole time...?

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.370
Honoka.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:59.080
Honoka, just focus on getting into college.

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:01.540
You want to work overseas in the future, right?

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:06.950
Aoi, you focus on getting into
the best high school for volleyball.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:09.830
Ichika, you don't have to worry
about anything yet.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.910
But just know, I'm going to work hard
so you can do anything you want!

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:17.040
And one more thing...

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.290
I want to wear this!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.000
Ikuto, what do you want to be when you grow up?

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.120
Yeah!

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.790
I know what I want to be!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.830
I...

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.080
I...

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:33.870
I want to be a fashion designer.

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.120
Okay.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.450
You can do it... Ikuto!

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.040
Mr. Yanagida.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.250
What is it?

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.250
Going back to this topic...

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:57.370
I want to be a designer because
I really love making clothes.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:02.660
I'm still not at the level
where I can dream big.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.000
But...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.290
There are people around me
who support my dream.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:12.450
And I'm determined to realize that dream.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:17.160
There are people I want to make clothes for.

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:22.830
It all stems from my love for making clothes.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.330
"Clothes that make people smile."

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.500
That's what I want to aim for as a designer.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.330
Will that count as an aspiration?

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.040
Sure, it's a great one.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:37.120
"Moriyama"

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:38.370
Huh?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.330
Got it.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:47.040
Did something happen?

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.620
Moriyama's quitting because her parents
are against her working here.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.370
What? So, the exhibition...

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.870
You're doing it. There's nobody else.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:57.160
What...?

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:03.500
And on top of that, Miss Moriyama quit!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.370
Miss Fujito, are you even listening?

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.410
Chiyuki.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:07.250
What?

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:11.620
It's about time you start calling me
by my first name.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.200
What?

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.540
Okay...

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:19.120
M-Miss Ch-Chiyu... ki...

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.200
But...

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:24.330
Well, good luck with that, Ikuto.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.290
Thank you.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.580
I'll do my best.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.410
<i>Smile Down the Runway</i>.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.370
Hello, welcome.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.040
Thank you very much.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.620
That's Sara, the famous model.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.870
There are so many celebrities here.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:50.160
May I give this to you?

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.620
Oh. Yes. Thank you very much.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.750
I know her!

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.870
She's Mai Ayano of Aphro I Dite!

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.620
She's one of the top designers in Japan.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:03.870
I can't believe it!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:07.790
Oh? I don't see the dress you fixed up.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.660
How do you know about that...?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.540
I heard from one of my students.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.620
They were helping out as a fitter.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:19.700
Hey, designer.
Have the model change into this piece.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.450
Yes, right away.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:23.790
He's got many faces...

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.660
Change into this right away.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.000
Yes, sir.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.540
Hey, help her out.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.700
What?

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:33.540
Why don't we have a changing room for her?

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:42.750
It's a cotton-based fabric processed
with polyester to mimic the texture of silk.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:47.290
It naturally accentuates
the lines of the female form.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:53.290
It's a simple yet versatile piece that can be
worn in both casual and formal settings.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:58.080
We'll allocate a booth for your brand
in our department store in two weeks.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:00.660
I need 40 types of seasonal pieces,

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:03.200
a total of at least 400 pieces.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.120
What?

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:04.660
--Four hundred pieces in two weeks?!

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.160
--Yes, thank you very much.
--Four hundred pieces in two weeks?!

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.450
Mr. Yanagida...

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.910
That...

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.290
Was his big break...

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:19.250
Bob. Go find the Geika principal
who was here earlier.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:21.120
We'll hire more help.

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.370
Earlier?

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:23.620
Am I being summoned?

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.580
Whoa!

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.330
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.410
I was listening.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:32.700
So how can I make the most
out of this transaction?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.750
I know! I'll coordinate the helpers,
so in exchange,

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:42.790
I want you to participate
in our school's fashion show.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:47.250
We're here.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.040
"Geika Fashion School"
This is Japan's premier fashion school,

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.040
Geika Fashion School!

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:59.580
The fashion show is part of the school festival.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:06.330
This year, at one student's request, I permitted
participants who aren't Geika students.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.290
Come in, come in.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:12.620
An exhibition of student works.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:13.830
Amazing.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.200
"Senior Toh Ayano"

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.620
"Senior Toh Ayano"
I see the same name over and over again.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.040
"Senior Toh Ayano"
I see the same name over and over again.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:23.540
Oh my, where did I put the application forms?

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.750
Huh?

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:32.330
Your three sizes are 82, 65, and 83.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.200
Did I get that right?

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.830
What?

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.080
Who the heck is he?!

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.790
Well hello, Toh!

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:41.660
It's been a while!

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.000
You're 105, 101, 105...

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.370
Did you gain weight, Principal?

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.870
Oh, my.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.660
I'm guessing he's our non-student participant?

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:54.700
That's right. How exciting, isn't it?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.500
Based on his bone structure,
he's about 17 or 18...

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:59.200
A high school student?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:03.370
That outfit. You're wearing
a school uniform button-up.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.950
The vest is handmade.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:08.040
Based on its wear,
a girl used to wear it regularly.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:12.830
Your bought those pants
but you hemmed them yourself.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:14.620
He's right about everything.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.830
He barely touched the clothes...

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.620
Principal, who is he?

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.200
Hey, it's Toh!

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.290
Hi, Toh!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:30.580
"Flirt"   "Squeeze"  "Flirt"
Oh, it's so good to see you, Toh!

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.410
"Flirt"   "Hehe"   "Flirt"
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:37.330
He's a particularly special student of mine.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:40.000
Out of this whole school, no,

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.700
maybe out of all the 120,000 students
who attended this school,

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:47.410
he probably stands on top of them all.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.290
"Senior Toh Ayano"

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.580
As a senior, that is.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.580
Excuse me.

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.790
Would you be interested in
interning at Hazime Yanagida?

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.370
No, he already works at Aphro I Dite.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:05.500
Sorry, I'm not interested in those things.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.620
I'm sorry.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.200
We're just desperate for some help...

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.040
Huh?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:14.660
Did you do something to
that lady's tunic by any chance?

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.370
It just feels

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:22.370
a little different from earlier
when she arrived.

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.000
It's because of this.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.750
I just took the decorative ribbon off the waist.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.790
You need to be more mindful
of the tunic's silhouette.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:36.830
The weight of the ribbon totally ruined it.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.750
Make sure you consult with the fabric
before you add anything like this.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.830
Thank you very much.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:47.080
He couldn't see the ribbon from his angle.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.790
He noticed the change
just by the look of the front.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:51.950
I change my mind.

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:52.790
Huh?

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:55.200
I'll help out with that brand.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.080
What?

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.700
It'll be fun with you around.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.290
If you can start tomorrow, that'd be great!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.290
Toh, are you sure about this?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:06.290
Of course I am, Shoko.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:07.950
Thanks again.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:12.200
I'm glad I requested
a non-student participant.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:14.290
This is going to be fun.

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:19.700
Hello.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.620
I'm sorry for being late.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.290
Huh?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.540
I'm Kokoro Hasegawa. I'm here to help out.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:31.160
The model from the other day?

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.540
Thank you for taking care of me the other day!

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:40.830
Oh! I'm sorry, I thought I recognized you.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.910
I didn't know we were expecting a model.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.160
Actually, I'm--

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.500
Please come in.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.450
Coming through!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:48.580
Mr. Ayano.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:51.950
Hey Ikuto and my darling freshman.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.250
You know who I am?

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.040
Of course I do.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:18:01.950
How could I not notice the freshman
with the most beautiful figure?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.250
A freshman?

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.620
You mean you're a freshman at Geika?

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:09.750
I'm Kokoro Hasegawa.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:13.830
I was a model that day,
but my real dream is to be a designer.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.500
I'm grateful to be here.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:18.620
I'm exempt from introducing myself, right?

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:19.870
Mr. Ikuto!

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.000
M-Mister?!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.580
You're younger but you have seniority here!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.620
She seems like a totally different person.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.910
Damn it. Things got a lot more complicated.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:31.500
Oh. The student helpers are here?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.370
Let's get right to--

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:36.830
I'm Toh Ayano, a senior at Geika.

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:40.500
Your three sizes are 86, 61, 86...

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:42.000
You've got a great figure--

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.250
Did you bring this one?

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:46.580
Wait, did you say Ayano?

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.750
You must be the rumored grandchild of Mai Ayano.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.200
What? You mean the top designer's...?

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:56.580
Having a famous grandmother
isn't without its troubles.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.910
Anyway, what's the complicated matter?

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:03.200
We're trying to fulfill an order of these shirts
made with special ordered material.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.040
It's processed to have a silky texture.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.250
It looks like silk but it's not as soft.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.250
The factory I usually use fell through.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:14.580
Then why don't you use real silk?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:15.700
What?

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.540
But that's why we special ordered that material.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.870
Silk is too soft, so it can't
achieve that silhouette.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.410
Do you have a good source for silk?

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:28.830
I can use my grandmother's connections.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:31.700
Is it possible to make that shirt with silk?

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.250
It is. There are two ways to go about it.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.620
Then shouldn't we discuss it and decide?

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.160
That's not how I work.

00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.700
I want the designer to maintain
their position at the top.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:45.660
The designer is the one
who comes up with the designs.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:48.120
On the other hand, we're merely
slaves to those designs,

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:53.120
it'd be unacceptable for us to contribute
to the design-making process.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.410
This guy's scary.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:57.870
I'll explain the process now.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:01.870
We're making a bias-cut shirt using Georgette.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:03.410
Jumping right into making the sample.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.410
Ayano. You know how to do it.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:09.330
Actually, it's not really hitting me right now.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:13.000
I think Ikuto should show us
how it's done first.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:13.830
What?

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.750
W-Wait a minute!

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.250
I don't know how to do it either! And plus--

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.040
Good luck with that, Ikuto.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.910
I'll do my best.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.370
Angle the fabric at 45 degrees!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.040
Use needles #7 and #9!

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.950
If you can't shape it on the table,
do it directly on the torso.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.370
Set it on the brown paper and cut it!

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.540
Don't let it shift!

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.620
I told you to keep the thread loose.

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.660
Um... Can I--?

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:40.200
Kokoro.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:48.910
The bias-cut technique he wants
uses the fabric at an angle.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.700
By doing so, it produces elasticity,
and when we use an iron to shape it,

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:55.830
we can achieve a beautiful body line.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.910
But...

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.790
It's really difficult.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:02.330
You don't know how to handle the Georgette.

00:21:02.330 --> 00:21:05.330
The elasticity produced by bias-cut
differs with each material.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.410
Since it's not properly calculated
in your head, it comes out warped.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:11.290
You're incompetent, stand back.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.040
Yes...

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.830
Play time's over. Ayano, hurry up and do it.

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.250
All right.

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:19.620
I got a good sense of his abilities.

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:22.370
But what I really want to know is...

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:24.540
Ikuto, watch carefully.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:30.040
This is my first time

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:33.830
watching a professional sew.

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.870
It's drastically different.

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.040
And voilà.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:43.290
I'm far from being a professional.

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:44.790
You passed.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:47.660
Next, use this to draw up
the patterns for the factory.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.910
I've got a suggestion for that.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.250
You do it, Bob.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.580
Me?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.040
I see.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:58.330
So he noticed, too...

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.700
It's done.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:06.160
Nice try.

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:10.200
You still don't have a good grasp
of the material's elasticity.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:14.450
This part should be a millimeter shorter
to avoid producing any wrinkles.

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:20.750
But it's quite an improvement
after just looking at the finished product.

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:27.200
He already has the "eyes" that took me 20 years
to get while I worked for Mai Ayano.

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:31.000
That's it for today. You two can leave.

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:34.160
Ayano, we need to talk regarding the factory.

00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:40.080
You're working for Mai Ayano, aren't you?

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:41.410
Are you planning on taking over?

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:42.750
No way.

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:45.620
I'll launch my own brand, eventually.

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:47.250
What a waste.

00:22:47.250 --> 00:22:53.040
But it's easier said than done.
I was also looking for a partner.

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:54.540
"Was"?

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:56.330
Hey, Hajime.

00:22:56.330 --> 00:23:00.620
Can I have Ikuto for my brand?

00:24:31.540 --> 00:24:33.950
Next, "Individual Styles."

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.950
"See you next time!!"
